-- tests-independent-2-open.l4: the independent test author's answers on which the text can be read two ways, and the encoding takes the other reading.
-- Each assertion below FAILS by design (expected-failed in check.sh, 4). Each is recorded in NOTES as a fork "assumed, not ruled": a lawyer decides which reading stands.

-- K2-006
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(3), as a controller, does this Regulation apply to my processing of personal data, where I am a Union institution, body, office or agency` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- C3-032
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(5), as a controller, may I refuse to act on a request that is manifestly unfounded or excessive` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- C3-036
#ASSERT `Under Article 12(6), as a controller, may I request additional information necessary to confirm the identity of the data subject` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- C3-052
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
